                            <a name="comment2845"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Two Lives Blurred
</h4>

<p>
This was so good on many levels. Especially as fellow journalists, the conflict Luis goes through - in his mind and on paper - is great to see, and what he eventually ends up doing, all the while still debating in his mind and using the camera as a way to help soothe his worries about getting too involved.<br />
<br />
Others may disagree, but I think he made the right decision in helping out (how could he not?) and striking the right balance. I'm curious what others think about his actions?
</p>
<div class="posted">Posted by:


		<a href="mailto:alrooj@gmail.com">Raja</a>
	

 at November 13,2007 12:40
</div>
